  "primary_subject_agency_ids": [],
  "summary": "Oregon lawmakers Rep. Willy Chotzen (D-Portland) and Rep. Alek Skarlatos (R-Winston) plan to introduce 2027 legislation that would ban Flock and other automated license plate reader cameras, building on 2026's SB 1516 which imposed a 30-day retention limit and vendor liability. Law enforcement groups and Flock are expected to oppose a full ban, while bipartisan concern over misuse grows nationally.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "My constituents have been clear with me that they want to be able to go about their lives without being surveilled, and we are quickly moving into a new age in which everything we do is being tracked",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "A blanket ban would take a proven investigative tool away from communities and officers who rely on it",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "allowing Oregonians to sue vendors of automated license plate readers and limiting the amount of time police may hold onto the data to 30 days",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    }
  ],
